    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Desmoid fibromatosis of the breast shows interlacing fascicles of spindle cells with elongated and compressed nuclei, with irregular extensions into the surrounding fibroadipose stroma. Immunhistochemistry shows positive reactivity of spindle cells for beta catenin (both nuclear and cytoplasmic) with negative staining for epithelial markers, CD34, p63, S100 and desmin.</p>",
